{
  "_meta": {
    "name": "codec prefs | gpu_class",
    "parents": [
      "gpu_class"
    ],
    "children": [
      "av1_enabled",
      "webm_encoder_enabled",
      "mediasource_webm",
      "mediasource_mp4"
    ],
    "source": "5 JS-visible codec/media prefs, joint-sampled given gpu_class. Modern/workstation GPUs bias toward latest-Firefox-defaults (all-on). Integrated_old skews toward mixed/conservative states (older FF builds, AV1 adoption lower).",
    "rationale": {
      "av1_enabled": "media.av1.enabled - JS-visible via HTMLVideoElement.canPlayType('video/webm; codecs=\"av01.0.05M.08\"').",
      "webm_encoder_enabled": "media.encoder.webm.enabled - JS-visible via MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported('video/webm').",
      "mediasource_webm": "media.mediasource.webm.enabled - JS-visible via MediaSource.isTypeSupported('video/webm; codecs=\"vp9\"').",
      "mediasource_mp4": "media.mediasource.mp4.enabled - JS-visible via MediaSource.isTypeSupported('video/mp4; codecs=\"avc1.42E01E\"').",
      "webspeech_synth": "media.webspeech.synth.enabled - JS-visible via ('speechSynthesis' in window). Triggers CreepJS voices probe."
    },
    "note": "Replaced hw_video_decoding/wmf_enabled/ffvpx_enabled (backend-only, invisible to JS fingerprinters) with these 3 JS-visible ones for actual media.$hash entropy gain.",
    "webspeech_synth_removed": "2026-09-15. It was drawn here (about 12% False) and never read: media.webspeech.synth.enabled is emitted as a constant True, which is retail Firefox's own desktop default, so a session answering False would have been the abnormal one. The draw only made Profile.codec.webspeech_synth contradict the pref the browser receives. Row order and probabilities are untouched - the key left every row's value, so the row a seed lands on, and every other field in it, are unchanged."
  },
